            <ArticleTitle>Persistence of primary empty sella syndrome despite obesity surgery: report of two unusual cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>875-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/02688697.2012.697215</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary empty sella syndrome (ESS) shares with idiopathic intracranial hypertension (IIH) high intracranial pressure (ICP) and association with obesity. Bariatric surgery is effective in IIH treatment; no data, however, exist about ESS. We report two overweight ESS patients in whom bariatric surgery resolved obesity but failed in curing ESS, requiring cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) shunt placement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
